From 400df9eb6a1e1749bc96043ccd059e8eaaae3a8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:05:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] test(floor): anchor the delivery verdict where it is
 formed now
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Red: a-floor-that-hears-the-compiler-but-not-the-browser
  ⛔ ORDERING — the rollback happens BEFORE the delivery verdict is formed
  (culprit 0e2ff096) -> { rollbackComesFirst: false, verdictFound: false }

Decision: P. 0e2ff096 widened the verdict from high findings to every open
finding: `const blockers = ((audit?.findings ...` became
`const openQualityFindings = ((audit?.findings ...` (blockers derived from
it) and the decision `const qualityDeliveryBlocked = ...`. Read the code
path: the runtime rollback (const runtimeBlockers) still sits inside the
self-QA block, before both; there is no return between them, and the
static_records mode (76f66a5d) runs the same audit -> rollback -> verdict
order (its records presentation sets no authored fallback, so the rollback
cannot misfire on it).

The test now anchors BOTH halves of the verdict — where the final audit's
findings are collected and where they decide delivery — and requires the
rollback before each.

Non-vacuity (move the verdict before the rollback, guard goes red, restore):
  floor-collect: `const openQualityFindings = ((audit?.findings ...` moved
  above AUTHORED_RENDER_FAULTS
    ✕ ⛔ ORDERING — the rollback happens BEFORE the delivery verdict is formed
    -   "rollbackComesFirst": true,  +   "rollbackComesFirst": false,
    RESTORED: sha256 identical
  floor-decide: a `const qualityDeliveryBlocked` formed above the rollback
    ✕ ⛔ ORDERING — the rollback happens BEFORE the delivery verdict is formed
    -   "rollbackComesFirst": true,  +   "rollbackComesFirst": false,
    RESTORED: sha256 identical

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CSeapUrWatvdumdAwyPuqV
---
 ...ears-the-compiler-but-not-the-browser.test.ts | 16 ++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/api/src/__tests__/a-floor-that-hears-the-compiler-but-not-the-browser.test.ts b/api/src/__tests__/a-floor-that-hears-the-compiler-but-not-the-browser.test.ts
index a5d000b8..1a753d5a 100644
--- a/api/src/__tests__/a-floor-that-hears-the-compiler-but-not-the-browser.test.ts
+++ b/api/src/__tests__/a-floor-that-hears-the-compiler-but-not-the-browser.test.ts
@@ -69,14 +69,22 @@ describe('the authored interface is rolled back by the browser, not only by the
 
     it('⛔ ORDERING — the rollback happens BEFORE the delivery verdict is formed', () => {
         //  This is the actual defect, and it is invisible to every other
-        //  assertion here. A rollback written after `blockers` is computed
+        //  assertion here. A rollback written after the verdict is computed
         //  would be perfectly correct code that nothing ever reaches in time.
+        //
+        //  The verdict is two lines now, and BOTH are anchored: the point where
+        //  the final audit's findings are collected, and the point where they
+        //  decide delivery. (Until 0e2ff096 it was one line,
+        //  `const blockers = ((audit?.findings`, reading high findings only;
+        //  every open finding blocks now, and `blockers` is derived from them.)
         const rollbackAt = SRC.indexOf('const runtimeBlockers');
-        const verdictAt = SRC.indexOf("const blockers = ((audit?.findings");
+        const collectedAt = SRC.indexOf('const openQualityFindings = ((audit?.findings');
+        const decidedAt = SRC.indexOf('const qualityDeliveryBlocked =');
         expect({
             rollbackFound: rollbackAt > 0,
-            verdictFound: verdictAt > 0,
-            rollbackComesFirst: rollbackAt > 0 && verdictAt > 0 && rollbackAt < verdictAt,
+            verdictFound: collectedAt > 0 && decidedAt > 0,
+            rollbackComesFirst: rollbackAt > 0 && collectedAt > 0 && decidedAt > 0
+                && rollbackAt < collectedAt && rollbackAt < decidedAt,
         }).toEqual({ rollbackFound: true, verdictFound: true, rollbackComesFirst: true });
     });
 
